  "body": "The [Make room admin](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/develop/docs/admin_api/rooms.md#make-room-admin-api) API allows a server admin to grant another user in the room the highest power level in that room. It seems to do this by high-jacking one of the user with the highest power level in the room, and use them to set the power level.\r\n\r\nThis will fail if the high-jacked user does not have the permission to change power level (for example in a room with no Admins). If it is somehow possible, it would be preferable to set the power level directly without high-jacking a user.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- Create a room\r\n- Add a couple users to the room\r\n- Demote yourself from \"Admin\" to \"Standard\"\r\n- Call the Make room admin API with a user id.\r\n\r\n### Homeserver\r\n\r\nPrivate university server\r\n\r\n### Synapse Version\r\n\r\n1.70.1\r\n\r\n### Installation Method\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Platform\r\n\r\nDo not know\r\n",
